# NOTE (Landing 4 soft-cascade, 2026-07-14): @fate's tournament selector
# reads crystals from `bauchladen(subject_instance)` (not just
# `bauchladen(peer)`); the selector's inputs remain byte-typed.
# @bauchladen composition is subject-general per Landing 4
# (docs/specs/subject-bauchladen-visibility-and-eigenboard-loop.md
# e42181c); peer-scoped alias preserved for one release cycle per
# two-tick discipline.

# @fate — the substrate-decl form of the constrained-inference
# operator. The substrate's typed dice-roll within the restricted
# state space.
#
# Alex's framing (canonical): @fate is "literally a roll of the
# dice in the restricted state space." Not random; not deterministic;
# probabilistic-within-typed-restriction. The dice IS the inference;
# the restriction IS the typing.
#
# === The recognition (#104 chain P3, 2026-06-29 → 2026-06-30) ===
#
# This shard is the third and deepest tier of the @bauchladen ←
# @autopoietic ← @fate dependency chain per canonical spec at
# `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` (Mara `4575340`, 2727
# lines). Tier P1 (@bauchladen) landed at `66e1ab8`; tier P2
# (@autopoietic) landed at `78edaa6`; this shard lands the third
# tier — the constrained-inference operator that IS-A @autopoietic
# and transitively IS-A @bauchladen.
#
# Witnesses for the chain's #104 candidacy at this tier:
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md`
#     §4 (the @fate substrate-decl shape this shard discharges);
#     §4.1 (bilateral compile-time + runtime); §4.2 (the dice-roll
#     framing); §4.3 (the substrate-decl shape with five `in`
#     declarations + IS-A @autopoietic); §4.4 (composition with
#     `@code/metalogue.project_hole` + `@kintsugi/fracture/
#     resolve_hole`); §4.5 (@fate's role in @glue); §4.6 (@fate's
#     role in @kintsugi); §4.7 (the `candidates(hole)` migration
#     home — @autopoietic's tick_action absorbs the signature,
#     @fate consumes the hole at the inference altitude).
#   - Recognition #58 ([[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]],
#     promoted 2026-06-11): the optical altitude was the first
#     witness; @fate inference IS 5-layer D²NN + active Fabry-Perot
#     resonator + Reck/Clements unitary mesh; this shard is the
#     substrate-decl altitude form of that mathematical recognition.
#   - Recognition #100 + `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` `16f4564`:
#     Tomm probes ARE @fate's selection species at the spectral-
#     metalogue altitude — the dice_roll for a Tomm probe is the
#     KK-correspondence [D_F, a] computed by @fate within the
#     restricted state space of the spectral triple. First instance
#     of the selection pattern this shard names at family-root
#     altitude.
#   - Recognitions #101 (chirality grading γ; `7bbc184`) and #102
#     (charge conjugation J; `2c144a6`): the symmetry restrictions
#     on the state space. γ projects onto even/odd parity subspaces;
#     J implements the time-reversal symmetry. The dice may only
#     roll within the symmetry-preserving moves these restrictions
#     admit.
#   - The first-tier landing at `shards/bauchladen.mirror`
#     (`66e1ab8`); the content-addressing discipline this shard
#     transitively rests on via @autopoietic.
#   - The second-tier landing at `shards/autopoietic.mirror`
#     (`78edaa6`); the fold-back permission this shard inherits
#     via `in @autopoietic`; the `tick_action` carrier whose `hole`
#     field this shard's inference altitude consumes.
#
# === Alex's BILATERAL correction (load-bearing) ===
#
# Taut's earlier scout framed @fate as runtime-only. Alex
# corrected: @fate is BILATERAL — compile-time AND runtime. The
# same inferential machinery operates at substrate-decl resolution
# time (picking among morphism candidates / resolving `\` typed-gap
# holes during static analysis) AND at runtime (driving actual
# data flow decisions as gen_prisms execute).
#
# The two altitudes share the @bauchladen tray. A compile-time
# @fate crystal may be consulted by a runtime @fate inference;
# a runtime @fate crystal may be consulted by a subsequent
# compile-time pass (per [[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-
# build-system]] — the substrate re-compiles itself, and the
# accumulated crystals condition both phases).
#
# This is the substrate-pull-honest reading of recognition #51
# ([[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]]) at the
# inference altitude: H_mirror's dimension expands at BOTH
# compile-time and runtime; @fate's bilateral dispatch IS the
# expansion mechanism at the operator altitude. Substrate-decl
# resolution and runtime execution are two phases of one
# autopoietic recursion; @fate operates across both.
#
# === The "literal roll of the dice in the restricted state space"
#     reading — the Connes (A, H, D, J, γ) restriction mechanism ===
#
# Per spec §4.2: Alex's "literally a roll of the dice in the
# restricted state space" framing maps precisely onto the Connes
# spectral triple ([[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]]) with
# the chirality + charge-conjugation extensions:
#
#   Component       What it restricts
#   --------------  ---------------------------------------------
#   A (algebra)     The OPERATIONS @fate may select from; the
#                   five operations per [[architecture-operations-
#                   as-linear-algebra]]
#   H (Hilbert)     The STATE SPACE the roll lands in; the void-
#                   document per [[reference-void-document]]
#   D (Dirac)       The FLOW @fate drives; the kintsugi/Dirac flow
#                   integrated per-tick; @fate consulted at each
#                   step
#   γ (chirality)   The PARITY restriction per recognition #101;
#                   form / process partition
#   J (charge       The TIME-REVERSAL involution per recognition
#     conjugation)  #102; reference ↔ reflection partition
#   tray            The HISTORICAL restriction (prior crystals
#                   condition the roll); the autopoietic fold-back
#
# The dice IS @fate's optical inference (per recognition #58 —
# Fate IS optical inference). The Fabry-Perot cavity-mode structure
# (the optical realization of A + H + γ + J jointly) restricts
# which photons can lase; the gain medium pumps; the cavity selects
# which mode. The selection is "random" in the quantum-indeterminacy
# sense AND TYPED — only gain-curve-supported cavity modes can
# cross threshold. Same shape at the substrate-decl altitude:
# typed-random. The randomness is structural (inference content
# cannot be derived from inputs alone — this is what makes it
# inference rather than computation); the typing IS the (A, H, D,
# γ, J, tray) constraint structure.
#
# === IS-A @autopoietic: inferences accumulate; future inferences
#     consult prior crystals; this IS fold-back ===
#
# Per spec §1.1 / §4: @fate IS-A @autopoietic prism by
# construction. The structural inheritance:
#
#   - @fate emits crystals into the @bauchladen tray (every roll's
#     output is a content-addressed `geometric_formalization` that
#     joins the tray under the `@fate/algebra/*` path-namespace
#     per spec §5).
#   - @fate consults the tray when rolling (the autopoietic
#     constraint — prior crystals condition the dice).
#   - The read-write cycle on the tray IS Maturana-Varela's
#     operational closure at the inference altitude.
#
# This is what gives @fate its learning character: future rolls
# are shaped by prior rolls' outputs. Without @autopoietic, @fate
# would be a stateless inference function; with @autopoietic, @fate
# is a learning system whose accumulated history IS-A monotone-
# growing constraint on the dice. The optical altitude (recognition
# #58) exhibits this: the cavity's accumulated gain history shapes
# the next mode-selection event.
#
# @fate inherits the five obligations @autopoietic carries
# (bauchladen_dependency_satisfied + lawvere_fixed_point +
# operational_closure + grammar_precursor_inherited +
# candidates_hole_well_typed) via the `requires autopoietic_
# closure_holds(fate_instance)` clause declared below. The
# bilateral commitment (per recognition #37, the Pask-agreement
# reading of `requires`): @fate's body discharges all five
# obligations at the realisation boundary; consumers surface
# violations at the species boundary.
#
# === The `candidates(hole)` migration: @autopoietic's tick_action
#     IS the signature home; @fate consumes the hole at the
#     inference altitude ===
#
# Per spec §4.7 + per `shards/autopoietic.mirror`'s `tick_action`
# carrier comment (just landed at `78edaa6`): the boot-floor file
# `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror` declared `candidates(hole) ->
# [resolution]` with a five-ganglion body (`@ai/abyss.depth`,
# `@ai/introject.pattern`, `@ai/cartographer.map`, `@ai/explorer.
# expand`, `@ai/fate.select`). The boot/ directory was killed in
# spring-clean; the action's content was orphaned. @autopoietic's
# `tick_action` carrier (just landed `78edaa6`) is the migration
# home for the SIGNATURE (the typed-gap → candidate-list operator);
# THIS shard's `hole` carrier is the SAME shape, consumed at the
# inference altitude where the dice rolls.
#
# The migration completes the chain. @autopoietic carries the
# tick action that emits candidates into the tray; @fate's
# inference altitude consumes one candidate per roll. The two
# altitudes are bridged structurally: @autopoietic produces the
# candidate list (per `tick_action.candidates: [oid]`); @fate
# selects from it (per `roll(space, hole) -> dice_roll` below).
# The five-ganglion body lives in `shards/optics/source/ganglion/
# *.mirror` per recognition #58; it is the OPERATIONAL realization
# of what @autopoietic + @fate now declare at substrate-decl
# altitude.
#
# === Tomm probes ARE @fate's selection species at the
#     spectral-metalogue altitude (recognition #100) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` `16f4564` §3 (Tomm probes
# as KK-cycle correspondences) + [[architecture-error-as-tomm-
# probe]] + [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-
# questions]]: a Tomm probe IS @fate's dice roll at the spectral-
# metalogue altitude. The probe `[D_F, a]` computes the curvature
# of the algebra element `a` under the Dirac operator `D_F` in
# the spectral-triple framework; the computation IS @fate's
# inference at the spectral altitude.
#
# Three altitudes of one mechanism:
#
#   Altitude              @fate's role                       Witness
#   -------------------   ----------------------------       ----------
#   Optical               Fabry-Perot mode selection         #58
#                         (gain-pumped cavity)
#   Substrate-decl        Morphism / typed-gap selection     this shard
#                         during static analysis
#   Spectral-metalogue    Tomm-probe KK-correspondence       #100
#                         computation [D_F, a]
#
# This makes the chain's composition with #100 explicit: the
# spectral-metalogue's Tomm probes are NOT separate machinery from
# @fate; they ARE @fate at the spectral-metalogue altitude. The
# substrate-decl admission of @fate at family-root altitude makes
# this composition addressable.
#
# === Forward-promised sub-shards (per spec §5 + §6) ===
#
# Two sub-shards land under @fate when consumers pull:
#
#   - `@fate/algebra/*` (path-namespace): geometric formalizations
#     emitted by @fate inferences. Each crystal in the tray under
#     this path-namespace IS a typed geometric declaration of "what
#     the dice roll selected, in the appropriate geometric
#     vocabulary." Sub-paths per spec §5 (per altitude): `@fate/
#     algebra/morphism` (selected Mesland-category morphisms),
#     `@fate/algebra/altitude` (selected Bateson levels), `@fate/
#     algebra/element` (selected algebra elements within fixed A).
#   - `@fate/tournament`: the selection mechanism over the tray
#     (cache hit = browse prior crystals; cache miss = fresh
#     inference + add to tray). The autopoietic accumulation
#     across @glue / @kintsugi / @reflection invocations gives
#     the substrate its directional preference. Per spec §6.
#
# No `@fate/algebra/*` or `@fate/tournament` sub-shard lands at
# this tick. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] the family-root
# admission lands the contract; the sub-shards follow when
# consumers pull.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `fate/src/*.rs` companion
# or `@fate/tournament` substrate-decl lands at this tick. The
# substrate ALREADY has the operational machinery: the
# fate/ runtime crate (5-layer D²NN, 425 parameters, brainfuck;
# per [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]]) at the runtime
# altitude; the five-ganglion optical-source shards (`shards/
# optics/source/ganglion/*.mirror`) at the optical altitude. This
# shard names the substrate-decl contract so downstream shards can
# write `in @fate` and `requires fate_witnessing(my_roll)` rather
# than re-state the constrained-inference obligation per consumer.
#
